{
  "stage": "write",
  "item": "ch05.s14",
  "inputs_hash": "97bb303e7dc0b7db514c0c7d128f2c296fd0ea53824ecc347d25bdadf7ab3df6",
  "output_hash": "5e6c51c6c6249d4d359b078b249eaa1f1228bc73f8434904e17c92e39a9188c0",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch05.s14",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p01.01",
            "text": "How does a fine-tuned spam classifier get used on messages it has never seen before, and why is that the step that matters now?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p01.02",
            "text": "After fine-tuning on supervised data and plotting the training and validation loss, the remaining step is to use the model on new data.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2319",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2322",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2324",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2326",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2328"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p01.03",
            "text": "The real test is performance on data the model has not seen before, because the goal is to judge how well it works as a spam classifier on unseen messages.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2351",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2353",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2355",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2357",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2360",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2367",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2368",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2371"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p01.04",
            "text": "At this final stage, the fine-tuned GPT-based model is used to classify spam messages.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2376",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2377",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2379",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2383",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2385"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p02.01",
            "text": "To make that possible, a function called \"classify_review\" takes any text and predicts whether it is spam or not.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2388",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2390",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2392",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2394"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p02.02",
            "text": "The first step is to convert the input text into token IDs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2413",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2415",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2417",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2429",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2431"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p02.03",
            "text": "The tokenizer used for this is the tiktoken tokenizer, described as a byte pair encoder that takes a sentence and converts it into a bunch of tokens.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2437",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2442",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2444",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2446",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2448"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p02.04",
            "text": "The model also needs its supported context length, which in this case is 1024.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2450",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2452",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2455"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p02.05",
            "text": "That context length is read from the positional embedding weight shape: the number of rows equals the context length, and the number of columns equals the embedding dimension.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2458",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2461",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2464",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2467",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2469",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2471",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2473",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2475",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2478",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2479",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2481"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p03.01",
            "text": "With token IDs and context length in hand, the next question is how long each input sequence should be.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p03.02",
            "text": "The working maximum length is chosen by comparing the maximum token-ID length found in the training set with the supported context length and taking the smaller of the two.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2484",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2486",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2488",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2490",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2492",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2494",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2496",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2498",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2516",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2517",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2519"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p03.03",
            "text": "If the training-set maximum length is greater than the context length, sequences are truncated to the context length.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2503",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2506",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2508",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2511",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2521",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2523",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2526",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2529"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p03.04",
            "text": "Otherwise, the maximum length from the training set is used.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2531",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2533",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2535"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p03.05",
            "text": "Ideally, this maximum length comes from the longest message in the training dataset, but if that exceeds the context length then the context length is used instead.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2586",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2588",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2591",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2593",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2594",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2596",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2598"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.01",
            "text": "A new message must then be adjusted to that chosen length before it can be passed to the model.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.02",
            "text": "If a new message is shorter than the chosen maximum length, it is padded with end-of-text tokens until it reaches that length.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2541",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2544",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2551",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2553",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2555",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2557",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2560",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2562",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2565",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2568",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2569",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2572"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.03",
            "text": "The end-of-text token used for padding is 50256.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2565",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2568",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2605",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2607"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.04",
            "text": "Padding every input sequence to the same length is important because batching requires every sentence to have the same number of token IDs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2574",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2576",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2579",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2581",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2583",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2586"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.05",
            "text": "After tokenization and padding, the input is converted into a tensor and a batch dimension is added before inference.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2600",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2602",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2605",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2607",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2609",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2613",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2615",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2619"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p04.06",
            "text": "For inference on a new text message, the trained model is used only after making sure that the token IDs match the maximum length.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2642",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2644",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2646",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2649",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2653",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2655",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2657",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2660",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2661"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p05.01",
            "text": "Once the input has the right shape, the model can produce a class prediction.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p05.02",
            "text": "During inference, the model produces logits for the last output token, and applying argmax yields the prediction of spam or not spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2620",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2622",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2624",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2627",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2636",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2638",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2639"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p05.03",
            "text": "For example, the message \"you are a winner you have been specially selected to receive ,000 cash or $2,000 reward\" is passed through \"classify_review\", and the model predicts spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2664",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2666",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2668",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2670",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2672",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2675",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2677",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2679",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2686",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2688",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2690",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2692",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2694"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p05.04",
            "text": "A second message, \"hey just wanted to check if we are still on for dinner tonight let me know\", is also passed through the model.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2697",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2699",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2701",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2703"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p05.05",
            "text": "The model predicts that this legitimate message is not spam, and these new text samples appear to show good performance.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2705",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2707",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2709",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2711",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2713",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2749",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2752"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s14.p06",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.01",
            "text": "A fine-tuned model is more useful when its parameters can be reused later.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.02",
            "text": "The model can be saved so that it does not need to be trained again.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2789",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2792",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2794",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2796",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2798"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.03",
            "text": "\"torch.save\" saves the model parameters for later use.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2801",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2803",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2808",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2811",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2813"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.04",
            "text": "\"torch.load\" loads previously saved model parameters from a specified path, and the loaded parameters can be used for inference or for further fine-tuning.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2813b",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2816",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2819",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2820",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2822",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2824"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.05",
            "text": "This saves time and effort.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2826",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2828"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.06",
            "text": "Fine-tuning is necessary here because without it the model made very bad predictions and could not correctly answer a prompt asking whether a text was spam with a yes-or-no response.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2849",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2852",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2854",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2862",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2864",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2865",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2867",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2869"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s14.p06.07",
            "text": "The same classification fine-tuning code can also be tried on other datasets, such as a heart disease dataset.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2878",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2880",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2881",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2884",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2947",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2949",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2951",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2953"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "invalid_citation_sentences": 0
  }
}
